id: 2
hanzi: 传说
pinyin: chuán shuō
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: legend; folklore; mythical story; it is said that; tradition
  es: leyenda; relato mítico; tradición popular; se dice que; según dicen

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a traditional story or folklore passed down through generations, often explaining cultural customs or historical origins | leyenda; relato tradicional transmitido oralmente a lo largo de generaciones | 古老传说 (ancient legend)
  2 | Verb | Standard | it is said; rumor has it; they say that | se dice; según cuentan; corre el rumor de que | 传说除夕有怪兽出没 (legend has it that a beast roamed on New Year's Eve)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 传说中国古代有一种凶猛的怪兽叫“年”，每到除夕夜便会从深海爬上岸伤害人畜。 | Chuánshuō Zhōngguó gǔdài yǒu yì zhǒng xiōngměng de guàishòu jiào "Nián", měi dào Chúxī yè biàn huì cóng shēnhǎi pá shàng'àn shānghài rén chù. | Legend has it that in ancient China there was a ferocious beast called "Nian", which would crawl ashore from the deep sea every New Year's Eve to harm people and livestock. | Según cuenta la leyenda, en la antigua China existía una fiera temible llamada "Nian" que cada víspera de Año Nuevo emergía de las profundidades marinas para dañar a personas y ganado.
  #2 | 民间文学研究表明，许多关于除夕习俗的传说不仅承载着神话色彩，更折射出早期人类战胜自然灾害的集体心理。 | Mínjiān wénxué yánjiū biǎomíng, xǔduō guānyú Chúxī xísú de chuánshuō bùjǐn chéngzài zhe shénhuà sècǎi, gèng zhéshè chū zǎoqī rénlèi zhànshèng zìrán zāihài de jítǐ xīnlǐ. | Research in folklore indicates that many legends surrounding New Year's Eve customs not only possess mythical qualities, but also reflect humanity's early collective psychology in conquering natural calamities. | Los estudios de literatura folclórica revelan que las leyendas sobre las costumbres de fin de año albergan elementos míticos y reflejan la psicología colectiva ancestral para superar los desastres naturales.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  民间传说 | folk legend; folklore
  古老传说 | ancient legend
  神话传说 | myths and legends
  美丽传说 | beautiful legend
  据传说 | according to legend; as the story goes
  流传传说 | hand down a legend; circulate a tale

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  流传千古 | liú chuán qiān gǔ | spread and endure through thousands of years
  传为美谈 | chuán wéi měi tán | pass on as an inspiring story or anecdote
  道听途说 | dào tīng tú shuō | hearsay; gossip picked up on the road
  自圆其说 | zì yuán qí shuō | justify one's own statement; make one's story coherent

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  传 | chuán | transmit; pass on; spread | transmitir; propagar; pasar | 亻 | person / human | 亻 (person passing messages) | 专 (zhuān, focused / phonetic in simplified) | 6 | 左右结构 | Simplified from traditional 傳. Shows a person (亻) holding rotating post-horses or records (專) to convey dispatches across territories. | A messenger (亻) designated exclusively (专) to carry urgent news across kingdoms, passing down ancient tales. | Un mensajero (亻) con la tarea exclusiva (专) de transportar despachos urgentes y relatos orales por todo el reino. | 35 | OQNI | 傳
  说 | shuō | speak; say; explain; talk | hablar; decir; relatar | 讠 | speech / words | 讠 (words, spoken articulation) | 兑 (duì, joyful exchange / phonetic) | 9 | 左右结构 | Simplified from 說. Speech radical 讠 combined with 兑 (exchange of joyful speech), articulating thoughts into spoken words. | Spoken words (讠) shared with delightful joy (兑) by village elders recounting wonders around the hearth fire. | Palabras orales (讠) narradas con deleite (兑) por los ancianos alrededor del fuego para fascinar a la aldea. | 55 | IVCR | 說

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: What one person passes down (传) through spoken words (说) becomes an enduring legend (传说).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Lo que una persona transmite (传) mediante palabras habladas (说) se convierte en una leyenda (传说) eterna.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Oral traditions in ancient China relied on storytelling (说) transmitted across generations (传). Legends like Nian (年兽) and the white-bearded immortal explained seasonal rituals, moral codes, and protective customs.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone 'chuán' (35) followed by high level 1st tone 'shuō' (55). When '传' is used in 'biography' (zhuàn), it is 4th tone (51), but in 'chuánshuō' it must remain 2nd tone (35).

