semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 传说 refers to folklore or traditional myth passed down orally across generations, or verbal hearsay ('it is said').
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 传说 vs. 神话 | shénhuà | 传说 (legend) is often anchored to specific historical times, folk figures, or real cultural rituals (such as the origin of New Year's Eve), whereas 神话 (myth) deals with primordial deities, cosmic genesis, and supernatural creation.
    2 | 传说 vs. 寓言 | yùyán | 传说 focuses on narrative folklore explaining origins of customs, whereas 寓言 is an instructive fable designed explicitly to impart a moral or philosophical lesson.
    3 | 传说 vs. 谣言 | yáoyán | 传说 is culturally valued oral heritage or benign hearsay, whereas 谣言 refers to harmful, unfounded, and misleading rumors deliberately or negligently spread.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在围炉夜话的冬日里，关于年兽的传说总能轻易拨动游子的心弦。口耳相传的故事不仅承载着先民对凶险的敬畏，更寄托了以智慧驱散厄运的勇气。古老传说早已化作文化基因，世代相传。 | Zài wéilú yèhuà de dōngrì lǐ, guānyú Niánshòu de chuánshuō zǒng néng qīngyì bōdòng yóuzǐ de xīnxxián. Kǒu'ěr-xiāngchuán de gùshì bùjǐn chéngzài zhe xiānmín duì xiōngxiǎn de jìngwèi, gèng jìtuō le yǐ zhìhuì qūsàn èyùn de yǒngqì. Gǔlǎo chuánshuō zǎoyǐ huàzuò wénhuà jīyīn, shìdài xiāngchuán. | During winter evenings around the hearth, legends of the beast Nian easily strike a chord in wandering hearts. Stories passed down by word of mouth carry ancestors' awe of peril and reflect the courage to disperse misfortune through wisdom. Ancient legends have long crystallized into cultural heritage passed through generations. | Alrededor del fuego en noches de invierno, las leyendas de la fiera Nian conmueven a quienes están lejos del hogar. Relatos orales que transmiten el respeto de los antepasados ante el peligro y la valentía de ahuyentar el infortunio con ingenio. Estas viejas leyendas integran el patrimonio cultural transmitido entre generaciones.
  #2 | 民俗学视角下的除夕传说，是农耕社会应对时间过渡危机的一套仪式化表达。通过对红布与爆竹声响的象征运用，传说将古人对凶险自然的恐惧转化为重构秩序的庆典，展现出强大的文化凝聚力。 | Mínsúxué shìjiǎo xià de Chúxī chuánshuō, shì nónggēng shèhuì yìngduì shíjiān guòdù wēijī de yí tào yíshìhuà biǎodá. Tōngguò duì hóngbù yǔ bàozhú shēngxiǎng de xiàngzhēng yùnyòng, chuánshuō jiāng gǔrén duì xiōngxiǎn zìrán de kǒngjù zhuǎnhuà wéi chónggòu zhìxù de qìngdiǎn, zhǎnxiàn chū qiángdà de wénhuà níngjùlì. | From a folkloric perspective, the New Year's Eve legend is a ritualized response of agrarian society to the crisis of temporal transition. Through the symbolic use of red cloth and firecrackers, the legend transmutes fear of nature's perils into celebrations that restore social order, demonstrating cultural cohesion. | Desde la perspectiva folclórica, las leyendas de fin de año constituyen una respuesta ritualizada de la sociedad agraria a la transición temporal. Mediante el uso simbólico de telas rojas y petardos, transforman el temor a los peligros naturales en festejos que restablecen el orden, mostrando gran cohesión cultural.